 ## Background
-Spot noise was introduced by van Wijk [vW91] and further developed by de Lavergtelle et al. [dLvL97] as a sparse convolution noise method [Lew89]. It is based on the idea of developing a pattern after many thousands of tiny drops, representing a flow field [S1, unofficial]. The method is defined as a sparse convolution noise with a flexible kernel formulation where a uniform distribution of impulses is convolved with an arbitrary kernel spatially defined [S2, unofficial].
